"""The "can flutter_rust_bridge be built by Bazel?" experiment.

Its own Bazel workspace root, for the same reason e2e/flutter_demo is one:
`bazel_frb` is listed in the repo root's `.bazelignore`, so nothing under it
is visible to `//...` at the root. Run every command in README.md from THIS
directory.

It deliberately does NOT `bazel_dep` on frustrate. The question is what
rules_rust and rules_dart alone can do with FRB's crate, FRB's generated Rust
and FRB's generated Dart, and a frustrate dep would only add noise.

NO .bazelrc, by repo rule: every diagnostic flag is passed on the command
line so that the command is the reproduction.
"""

